  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Ben O'Steen noted in ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "url": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-522#icft=FCREPO-522"
       },
       "type": "inlineCard"
      },
      {
       "text": " that the .xml shortcut is problematic for the REST API's /objects/pid/datastreams/{dsid} (apim:getDatastream, which gets datastream metadata) endpoint.  It's problematic when the datastream id ends with .xml.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "We discussed this on the Sept15th call and decided to get rid of the .xml shortcut as a solution.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This issue is to extend that, for consistency, across the REST API.  There are places where it's NOT problematic from a functional perspective, but the lack of consistency would be troubling from a design perspective.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
